WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.988
Start with what we're actually measuring.

2
00:00:01.988 --> 00:00:06.036
An app can hold two kinds of
permission: an application permission,

3
00:00:06.036 --> 00:00:09.569
which is a role it holds on
another app's service principal,

4
00:00:09.569 --> 00:00:14.426
and a delegated permission, which is a
grant to act for one person or for everyone.

5
00:00:14.426 --> 00:00:17.926
Learn's way to see what an app
can reach is to walk every service

6
00:00:17.926 --> 00:00:22.113
principal's role assignments, paying
close attention to Microsoft Graph.

7
00:00:22.113 --> 00:00:26.288
And remember that directory roles
and mail roles grant access too.

8
00:00:26.288 --> 00:00:30.870
For this estate, everything goes to the
worldwide Graph and commercial Azure,

9
00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:34.510
and every call is available in
the government clouds as well.
